<title>USA: Central U.S. carlot beef trade 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>Central U.S. carlot beef trade 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cow and bull carcasses not established, according to USDA.</p>
<p>COW &amp; BULL CARCASS CAF WEST COAST  Nil Loads Reported.</p>
<p>			  Lds     Price Range    Latest Estb. Mkt.</p>
<p>UT,brk 2-4 450#/up				  68.00 C</p>
<p>UT,bng 1-3 400#/up				  70.00 - 71.00 B</p>
<p>Cutter 1-2 350#/up				  70.00 B</p>
<p>Bulls YG 1 500#/up				  unq</p>
<p>BONELESS PROCESSING BEEF/BEEF TRIMMINGS   49.0  Loads Reported.</p>
<p>Lean boneless processing beef not established in the Midwest, but Texas steady; 85% steady to weak; 65% weak. Demand light for moderate offerings. Beef trimmings generally lower on light to moderate demand and moderate to heavy offerings.</p>
<p>FOB OMAHA BASIS:</p>
<p>Chm Ln   Lds     Price Range		     Wtavg</p>
<p>90% fr	  93.0 -  93.5			93.30 C</p>
<p>90% fz	 100.0 - 102.0		     101.29 B</p>
<p>85% fr    5   88.0 -  89.0			88.40</p>
<p>65% fr    3	     63.0			63.00</p>
<p>50% fr   23  38.00 - 45.00			42.24</p>
<p>50% fz   15	    45.00			45.00</p>
<p>FOB EAST TEXAS AND OKLAHOMA:</p>
<p>90% fr    3	     94.0			94.00</p>
<p>CAF NORTHEAST AREAS:</p>
